# Opt-in Pika policy, below native Debian and installed versions (100).
# Select an initial package explicitly with apt install PACKAGE/pika.
# Later Pika versions can update that package; this never forces downgrades.
# To keep one package on Pika even if another archive publishes a newer build,
# add a package-specific origin pin (priority 990); APT does not record origins.

Package: *
Pin: release n=pika,c=cockatiel
Pin-Priority: 100

Package: *
Pin: release n=pika,c=nest
Pin-Priority: 100

Package: *
Pin: release n=pika,c=raven
Pin-Priority: 100

Package: *
Pin: release n=pika,c=pigeon
Pin-Priority: 100

Package: *
Pin: release n=pika,c=parrot
Pin-Priority: 100

Package: *
Pin: release n=pika,c=canary
Pin-Priority: 100

Package: *
Pin: release n=pika,c=nest-testing
Pin-Priority: 100

Package: *
Pin: release n=pika,c=cockatiel-testing
Pin-Priority: 100
